.TH MACHCTL 1 "November 2, 2026" "Mach 0.15.0" "Machctl Manual"
.SH NAME
machctl \- administrative control plane for Mach Linux machines, containers,
and Kubernetes
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B machctl
[\fIcommand\fR] [\fIflags\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B machctl
is the management CLI for \fBMach\fR, providing controls for Linux virtual
machines, OCI container integration, Kubernetes clusters, Apple Silicon
Rosetta 2 translation, networking, and system diagnostics.

.SH LINUX MACHINE COMMANDS
.TP
.BI create " [" distro "] [" name "] [" options "]"
Create a new Linux virtual machine.
Options:
.RS
.TP
.BI distro
Linux distribution (\fIdebian\fR, \fIubuntu\fR, \fIfedora\fR, \fIalpine\fR).
Defaults to \fIubuntu\fR. The machine name defaults to the distro name, with a
numeric suffix if needed.
.TP
.BI \-c " " cpus ", " \-\-cpus " " cpus
Number of virtual CPUs (defaults to 2).
.TP
.BI \-m " " memory ", " \-\-memory " " memory
Memory allocation in MiB (defaults to 2048 MiB).
.TP
.BI \-d " " disk ", " \-\-disk " " disk
Virtual disk size in GiB (defaults to 20 GiB). APFS Copy-on-Write ensures only
written blocks consume actual disk space.
.RE

.TP
.BI list ", " ls
List all configured Linux machines with their distribution, runtime status,
configured CPU/memory/disk allocations, and IP addresses. Protected system
machines require \fB--system\fR or \fB--all\fR.

.TP
.BI start " [" name "]"
Boot a stopped virtual machine into the background.

.TP
.BI stop " [" name "] [" \-\-force "]"
Gracefully shut down a running machine (or immediately terminate with
\fB\-\-force\fR).

.TP
.BI restart " [" name "]"
Restart a running virtual machine.

.TP
.BI delete " " name " [" \-\-yes "]"
Delete a virtual machine and its associated APFS disk image.

.TP
.BI clone " " source " " target
Clone a stopped machine using APFS Copy-on-Write where supported, with a
file-copy fallback. Shared disk blocks consume additional space as they are
modified; metadata and other copied files also require space.

.TP
.BI rename " " old_name " " new_name
Rename an existing machine.

.TP
.BI info " [" name "]"
Display human-readable metadata for a machine (IP address, MAC
address, vCPUs, RAM, disk allocation, APFS physical footprint).

.TP
.BI top " [" \-\-interval " " seconds "]"
Interactive live terminal dashboard displaying host VMM process CPU usage,
resident memory (RSS), APFS CoW disk savings, and host resource utilization.

.TP
.BI ssh " [" name "]"
Display SSH connection credentials and helper commands for a machine.

.TP
.BI push " [" \-m " " machine "] " source " " destination
Copy files or directories from macOS to the Linux guest.

.TP
.BI pull " [" \-m " " machine "] " source " " destination
Copy files or directories from the Linux guest to macOS.

.TP
.BI export " " machine " " output_archive
Export a stopped machine as a raw disk file and a separate JSON
\fB.mach-meta\fR sidecar. Keep both files to preserve machine configuration.

.TP
.BI import " " input_disk " " name
Import a raw disk file under the required machine name, reading its
configuration sidecar if present.

.TP
.BI default " [" name "]"
Get or set the active default machine used by \fBmach\fR.

.TP
.BI mount " " name " [" path "]"
Mount a Linux machine's filesystem or open it in macOS Finder
(\fB~/Mach/machines/<name>\fR).

.SH CONTAINER & KUBERNETES COMMANDS
.TP
.BI docker " start [" \-\-system "]"
Start the Docker engine inside the system infrastructure VM and configure the
macOS Docker CLI context. With \fB\-\-system\fR, creates a system-wide symlink
at \fB/var/run/docker.sock\fR.
.TP
.BI docker " stop"
Stop the Docker engine and terminate background socket forwarding.
.TP
.BI docker " restart"
Restart the Docker engine.
.TP
.BI docker " logs [" \-f "] [" \-n " " N "]"
View Docker daemon system logs.
.TP
.BI docker " status"
Display current Docker daemon status and API responsiveness.

.TP
.BI k8s " enable"
Provision and start K3s in the shared infrastructure VM using its own
containerd. Docker images are not automatically shared with this runtime.
Automatically configures \fB~/.kube/config\fR.
.TP
.BI k8s " disable"
Disable the local Kubernetes cluster and terminate API forwarding.
.TP
.BI k8s " restart"
Restart the Kubernetes cluster.
.TP
.BI k8s " logs [" \-f "] [" \-n " " N "]"
View Kubernetes (K3s) daemon system logs.
.TP
.BI k8s " status"
Display Kubernetes cluster health and node status.

.TP
.BI debug " " container_name
Drop an interactive debugging shell into a Docker container with preloaded
networking and diagnostic utilities.

.SH NETWORKING & SYSTEM COMMANDS
.TP
.BI doctor
Run comprehensive health checks on virtualization hardware, entitlements, APFS
CoW support, SSH keys, Docker sockets, and DNS resolvers.

.TP
.BI dns " enable | disable | status"
Configure the native macOS resolver for \fB*.mach.local\fR domains via
\fB/etc/resolver/mach.local\fR.

.TP
.BI tls " install [" \-\-system "]"
Generate and trust a local wildcard TLS certificate authority in the macOS
Keychain for trusted HTTPS across browsers and curl.

.TP
.BI daemon " start | stop | status"
Manage the background async port forwarding and DNS routing daemon.

.TP
.BI uninstall " [" \-\-all "] [" \-\-force "] [" \-\-keep\-data "]"
Completely uninstall Mach, stop all VMs and daemons, reset Docker and
Kubernetes contexts, restore ~/.ssh/config, remove TLS certificates, and clean
up ~/.mach data.

.TP
.BI version
Print version, build profile, and target architecture.

.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B Create an Ubuntu machine with 4 vCPUs and 4 GB RAM
machctl create ubuntu dev-box --cpus 4 --memory 4096
.TP
.B Clone a stopped machine
machctl clone dev-box dev-box-backup
.TP
.B Launch Kubernetes cluster
machctl k8s enable
.TP
.B Verify system health
machctl doctor

